Figure 8, printed in the document with the caption "Figure 9". Two stacked bars, "Baseline" and "Advanced RTU Controls", on a y-axis "Annual Energy Consumption (TBtu)" running 0 to 4500, with a legend of 18 end-use-by-fuel segments (interior equipment, fans, cooling, interior lighting, heating, water systems, exterior lighting, refrigeration, pumps, heat rejection and heat recovery, each split by electricity, natural gas, district heating or cooling, and other fuel). This is the whole modelled stock, including buildings the measure was not applicable to. The bar totals are 4338 TBtu baseline and 4156 TBtu with the measure, a reduction of 182 TBtu or 4.2%. Fan electricity falls from 519.1 to 382.0 TBtu (-137.1, the largest single contribution) and cooling electricity from 667.3 to 643.3 TBtu (-24.0); natural gas heating falls by 18.1 TBtu (2.1%) per the body text, though that segment's printed label is illegible in this bitmap. Heating electricity edges down from 175.2 to 173.6 TBtu. Interior equipment electricity (739.7) and interior lighting (451.9) are unchanged. For per-segment numbers, see the section 5.2 bullets.

