for applicable buildings only, baseline versus Advanced RTU Controls, by end use and fuel type.](89117_images/image_000015_832e196c03d5d62d9ed3542f0294a0129b10d309843368da0349c26fb3b61ba6.png)

Figure 9, printed in the document with the caption "Figure 10". The same stacked-bar format as Figure 8 - "Baseline" and "Advanced RTU Controls" bars, y-axis "Annual Energy Consumption (TBtu)" 0 to 1800, segments by end use crossed with fuel type - but restricted to the buildings the measure was applicable to, which the text offers as a more direct basis for comparison with field studies. The bar totals are 1774 TBtu baseline and 1591 TBtu with the measure, a reduction of about 183 TBtu or roughly 10% of this subset's energy use. Fan electricity falls from 268.8 to 131.6 TBtu and cooling electricity from 243.9 to 220.0 TBtu; both deltas match the stock-level savings in Figure 8, confirming that essentially all of the savings arise in these buildings. Natural gas heating also falls, by 6.1% per section 5.2, although that segment's printed label is illegible in this bitmap. Interior equipment electricity (289.1), interior lighting (199.6), exterior lighting (65.1) and gas water systems (76.9) are unchanged. Section 5.2 gives the end-use percentages: 53.3% fan savings, 11.2% cooling, 6.1% gas heating.

